AB  - With edge computing, one can scale the CPS applications and ensure the safety of diverse safety-critical systems with more autonomy. This chapter presents a tutorial, providing a holistic investigation of the relevance of edge computing concepts in the design of CPS and their application domains. A generic problem space is proposed to represent the representative CPS domains, the objectives facilitated by edge computing in CPS, and areas of challenges that require attention. Finally, state-of-the-art projects from academia and industry have been reviewed, and future research directions have been provided to indicate the significance of current work and the scope of research for future research efforts.
